    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7940",
      "problem": "Find the equation that generated the graph below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/16cbb1865575a8f1d968a065a3b9a09eb6fa3b998a24029d75713825cd5b7a2a.png)",
      "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/78b19415feaf4e648e0d49a7aa3a130db5a57cf23b4aeafbdc34e5a968a3bf0e.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the left by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\n- Translate the result up by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x+1}+2.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/4ffbc7f9dd9ec50830a671f4ce688f51f6a7a11663f0c93af567ee8cc9a4a4f4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y = -\\sqrt{x+1}+2.$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/observations/step-e7940-33d2c20d0016ccb24a4a.html",
